{
  "name": "iOS — Journey vs Crashes by Screen (guided)",
  "tabs": [
    {
      "name": "Guided analysis",
      "stylistic_components": [
        {
          "id": "t-intro-h",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "iOS — which journeys lead to crashes?",
            "variant": "h2"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-intro-p",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "A crash can't be the final node of a Sankey on iOS, so this dashboard splits the question in two and joins it on screen name: the funnel and Sankey show where journeys die, the rate chart shows where the app dies.",
            "variant": "p"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 3,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 4
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-s1-h",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Start here — which screen is actually risky?",
            "variant": "h3"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 7,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-s1-p",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Crash rate per screen: terminations on a screen divided by visits to it. Read the top bar, then find that screen in the Sankey and follow its inbound bands — those are the journeys leading into the crash. That is the whole analysis. Raw counts (section 3) mostly rank popularity: Cart and Confirmation can show similar counts while Cart has several times the rate.",
            "variant": "p"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 10,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 5
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-s2-h",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Where journeys drop off",
            "variant": "h3"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 28,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-s2-p",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Read these two together: the funnel bars are the Sankey columns, left to right. The funnel tells you how many survive each stage; the Sankey tells you which routes they took and where they branched. A stage that loses volume in the funnel AND has a high crash rate above is a crash-driven leak; losing volume with a near-zero crash rate is UX, not crashes.",
            "variant": "p"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 31,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 5
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-s3-h",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Raw crash detail",
            "variant": "h3"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 62,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-s3-p",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Counts by the screen the user was on when the previous run died, reported next launch from a persisted field — which is how it catches hangs and OOM kills. Filter reason to fatalCrash for real crashes. 'other' means the app died before reaching any screen.",
            "variant": "p"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 65,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 4
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-how-h",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Caveats",
            "variant": "h3"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 81,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-how-p",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Correlational, not causal. Attribution is to the last screen reached, so a background crash still lands on whatever was visible. Session rotation is on (one per journey), so treat per-session rates as a demo artifact.",
            "variant": "p"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 84,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 4
          }
        }
      ],
